// =============================================================================
// credit/js/deal-tags.js — curated per-deal TAGS for the Transactions filters
// (HOUSE_STYLE R39). Kept apart from data.js so the refresh routine can append a
// new deal's tags without touching the deal ledger. Every tag is read from the
// deal's OWN sourced headline / summary — never guessed; unknown = null.
//   country    — where the borrower / asset / target is (not the lender's HQ). Read from
//                the deal's own text; where the text is silent, researched from a public
//                source (company site, registry, filing, press) and recorded with
//                cs = that source URL and cb = "hq" | "incorporated" (an operating
//                borrower), "issuer" (a CLO / CFO / fund / vehicle's domicile — Irish DAC,
//                Luxembourg SCSp, Cayman Ltd, Delaware LP …) or "portfolio" (where a
//                traded loan portfolio's assets are) (2026-10 back-fill).
//   sector     — the borrower's industry (SECTOR_TAGS order below)
//   amountKind — what the parsed amount measures: financing | fund | portfolio |
//                ev | aum | other (only financing / fund / portfolio count as deal size)
//   event      — CLO issuance only: new | reset | refi
//   managerMA  — true when the deal is the acquisition of / stake in an asset manager
//   party (p)  — the audited counterparty for the "Borrower / issuer" column, verbatim
//                from the deal's own headline/summary ("" = none), with its role (r):
//                borrower | issuer (incl. a BDC / manager issuing its own notes, a CLO
//                vehicle) | target | fund | seller | none. Wins over the headline parse
//                in v2/js/deal-parse.js (2026-10 audit of every deal). Where the text
//                doesn't name it (an unnamed CLO vehicle, a seller's subsidiary), `p`
//                was researched and `ps` holds the source URL (shown in the drawer).
//                pq marks a weaker party: "unconfirmed" (inferred, e.g. from a series'
//                numbering — shown with an asterisk) or "placeholder" (no source names
//                the vehicle — "<Manager> vehicle").
// =============================================================================
// Compact keys (c country · s sector · a amountKind · e event · m managerMA) — expanded
// by tagsOf() in credit/js/tx.js. Tagged 2026-10 from each deal's own text.
